<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk oil port remains closed.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk oil port remains closed.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's leading oil export terminal at Novorossiisk on the Black Sea remained closed on Friday due to a heavy swell and high winds, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>Bad weather has kept the port closed for much of February, leading to loading delays of about five days, traders said.</p>
<p>Other Black Sea oil ports at Odessa and Tuapse were operating normally, as was Latvia's Ventspils terminal on the Baltic Sea, the source said.</p>
